According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text'. In the input, the object A is inside the code fence, so it is the scored object. The object B is outside the fence. In the rewritten text, the object B is removed, but the code fence still holds object A. Thus the recovered object stays unchanged.